<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for the Developer ID signed build.
  Notarization requires the hardened runtime; Sparkamp needs no exceptions to
  it, so this grants none.

  It used to grant `allow-unsigned-executable-memory`, because GStreamer's
  liborc JIT-compiled its SIMD kernels into RWX pages at runtime and the
  hardened runtime forbids that. No GStreamer ships in the macOS build any
  more — audio is AVFoundation — so the exception went with it rather than
  being left behind as a permission nothing uses.

  The app is deliberately NOT sandboxed: it shells out to drutil for disc
  burning, reads arbitrary /Volumes paths for device sync, and watches
  user-chosen library folders. Developer ID distribution does not require the
  App Sandbox. The Mac App Store build is a different signing pass with
  entitlements-appstore.plist, and that one IS sandboxed.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
